     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">pls follow <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/07/how-to-bug-author/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/07/how-to-bug-author/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482584406000&amp;usg=AOvVaw135owCuhNi0fy2sYm_Lz9t\">https://guangchuangyu.github.io/2016/07/how-to-bug-author/</a> and provide a reproducible example if the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">ladderize</code> didn’t work using latest release version.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:cGxzIGZvbGxvdyAmbHQ7aHR0cHM6Ly9ndWFuZ2NodWFuZ3l1LmdpdGh1Yi5pby8yMDE2LzA3L2hv\r\ndy10by1idWctYXV0aG9yLyZndDsgYW5kIHByb3ZpZGUgYSByZXByb2R1Y2libGUgZXhhbXBsZSBp\r\nZiB0aGUgYGxhZGRlcml6ZWAgZGlkbid0IHdvcmsgdXNpbmcgbGF0ZXN0IHJlbGVhc2UgdmVyc2lv\r\nbi48YnI+PGJyPjxicj4=\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Mar 7, 2018 at 12:51 AM, 王大大 <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sunya...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Does ggtree have &quot; increasing node order&quot;and&quot; decreease node order&quot; function?<span><br><br>在 2018年3月7日星期三 UTC+8上午12:36:36，王大大写道：</span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">hi,everyone<span><div>I want to change the tree structure of tree From A TO B by ggtree. &quot;p &lt;- ggtree(tree, color=&quot;black&quot;, size=0.5, linetype=1,ladderize=TRUE)&quot; was used  and didn&#39;t work ,do  you have idea?</div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DFA3NZrEdn4/Wp7CzIRWH4I/AAAAAAAAAAk/MoGjF85RcCUSImEXcuGQjw0rtIcN7kOhACLcBGAs/s1600/A.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DFA3NZrEdn4/Wp7CzIRWH4I/AAAAAAAAAAk/MoGjF85RcCUSImEXcuGQjw0rtIcN7kOhACLcBGAs/s1600/A.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482584406000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06s21Bj987lPj8Czgdmit2\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DFA3NZrEdn4/Wp7CzIRWH4I/AAAAAAAAAAk/MoGjF85RcCUSImEXcuGQjw0rtIcN7kOhACLcBGAs/s320/A.png\" height=\"260\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\"></a></p><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vECv1uaw7OA/Wp7C64ob-cI/AAAAAAAAAAo/tGWf7BDXelo_ebUvW7wbZJPEG2pD-fdugCLcBGAs/s1600/B.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vECv1uaw7OA/Wp7C64ob-cI/AAAAAAAAAAo/tGWf7BDXelo_ebUvW7wbZJPEG2pD-fdugCLcBGAs/s1600/B.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482584406000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2FRLslvFz_OgVcNQI9Xqfr\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vECv1uaw7OA/Wp7C64ob-cI/AAAAAAAAAAo/tGWf7BDXelo_ebUvW7wbZJPEG2pD-fdugCLcBGAs/s320/B.png\" height=\"268\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\"></a></p></span></div></blockquote></div><span>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nG Yu, DK Smith, H Zhu, Y Guan, TTY Lam*. ggtree: an R package for visualization and annotation of phylogenetic trees with their covariates and other associated data, Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 2017, 8(1):28-36. doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12628<br>\r\n <br>\r\nHomepage: <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US